# Long horizontal video (~10–11 min): why physicists say time may not exist (or not be fundamental).
# Sources (checked):
#  - Augustine, Confessions, Book XI ("What then is time? If no one asks me, I know...").
#  - Einstein, letter to Besso's family, 21 Mar 1955: "the distinction between past, present and future is only a
#    stubbornly persistent illusion" (one of several translations; Quote Investigator 2024). Besso died 15 Mar 1955;
#    Einstein died 18 Apr 1955.
#  - Muons: mean lifetime ~2.2 μs; Frisch & Smith (Mount Washington, 1962; Am. J. Phys. 31, 1963): ~563 muons/h at the
#    summit, ~412/h at sea level vs ~27 expected without time dilation (factor ≈ 8.8).
#  - Hafele & Keating (Oct 1971; Science 177, 1972): eastward −59 ± 10 ns, westward +273 ± 7 ns.
#  - GPS: satellite clocks +45 μs/day (gravity) −7 μs/day (speed) ≈ +38 μs/day; uncorrected error ~10 km per day.
#  - Relativity of simultaneity; "block universe" / eternalism (Minkowski spacetime, 1908).
#  - Wheeler–DeWitt equation (DeWitt 1967): Ĥ|Ψ⟩ = 0, no time parameter — the "problem of time" in quantum gravity.
#  - Julian Barbour, "The End of Time" (1999): only timeless configurations ("Nows") exist.
#  - Page & Wootters (1983): time emerges via entanglement with a clock; Moreva et al., arXiv Oct 2013,
#    Phys. Rev. A 89, 052122 (2014): two entangled photons, global state static, one photon serves as a clock.
#  - Boltzmann: entropy and the arrow of time; Carlo Rovelli, "The Order of Time" (It. 2017, Eng. 2018); thermal time
#    hypothesis (Connes & Rovelli 1994) — told as hypotheses.
#  - J. M. E. McTaggart, "The Unreality of Time", Mind 17 (1908): A-series vs B-series.
#  - Brain: conscious perception of "now" lags real events by a fraction of a second (told generally).

def S(bg, *people, z=None, **kw):
    xs = {0: [], 1: [540], 2: [330, 750], 3: [280, 540, 800]}[len(people)]
    zoom = z or (1.3 if len(people) <= 1 else 1.1)
    return dict(bg=bg, cast=[(w, x, p) for (w, p), x in zip(people, xs)], cam=(zoom, 540, 1050 if zoom < 1.6 else 930), **kw)
def P(who, expr="neutral", **pose): return (who, dict(expr=expr, **pose))
